 "questions": [
  {
   "id": 520193,
   "is_answer_order_important": true,
   "stimulus_html": "",
   "stem_html": "<p><img src=\"exercises/media/c04448970b2df7fc.jpg\" alt=\"Table with four columns and two rows. Top, left header reads: Plate A. Top, middle header reads: Plate B. Top, right header reads: Plate C. Second row, left header reads: Percentage germination. Second row under Plate A reads: 95%. Second row under Plate B reads: 50%. Second row under Plate C reads: 52%.\"></p>\n\n<p>Seeds were germinated in the dark on three plates. Plate A was irradiated with a short pulse of red light; plate B was irradiated with a short pulse of red light followed by a pulse of far-red light; and plate C was the control and was maintained in the dark. After three days, the plates were scored for percentage of germination, as shown in this table.\n What conclusion can be drawn from the experiment?</p>\n",
   "answers": [
    {
     "id": 1016251,
     "content_html": "Darkness inhibits germination."
    },
    {
     "id": 1016252,
     "content_html": "Red light promotes germination."
    },
    {
     "id": 1016253,
     "content_html": "Far-red light promotes germination."
    },
    {
     "id": 1016254,
     "content_html": "Germination is independent from light irradiation."
    }
   ],
